 "answer": "On Windows, Ollama writes its server logs to:\n\n**`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama\\server.log`**\n\nThat usually expands to `C:\\Users\\<your-username>\\AppData\\Local\\Ollama\\server.log`. You can open it by pressing Win+R, entering `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama`, and opening `server.log`, or by running `explorer %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama` in PowerShell.\n\nThe same folder also contains `app.log`, which covers the Ollama desktop app, and `upgrade.log`. I believe older server logs are rotated into files such as `server-1.log`, but I'm not certain of the exact naming, so check the folder listing if you need an older run.",
